      "parentFingerprint": "d96370968d620efc86863f7ef4bfe2fbe2bf70f076b61a6cc812db6e40c62946",
      "passageSha256": "a04aae8a3633e4b55356ec0c3e076cc05fa4c40a78343e251365707d95fac672",
      "pdfPages": [
        157
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 14,
      "questionId": "qe-c13-0135",
      "sentenceId": "c13-s06-p157-02700-s001",
      "sentenceText": "With the Beatles, Bob Dylan, and Aretha Franklin, you can go deep and always find something new, as they left abundant, diverse bodies of work.",
      "sentenceSha256": "ee369892598f192db791d863176c54a9859f0d6d9dfa22da6a710fd5b0b73a33",
      "readingUnitId": "c13-s06-p157-02700-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c13-087",
      "parentFingerprint": "a68101c0f5088649ac3120574da8c8f7c4485d804cf5ba7c7c19cabf465e9c4d",
      "passageSha256": "b9587c4a6ff6408d50b736961c08e272ecf9781ced8c9c94e3014ed064e3d2b2",
      "pdfPages": [
        157
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 15,
      "questionId": "qe-c13-0136",
      "sentenceId": "c13-s06-p157-02700-s003",
      "sentenceText": "Many people keep listening to the same bands because of nostalgia.",
      "sentenceSha256": "026c1d5b8cc98564975d4795b96fe3c194e8338d64a0f50c4c9bd92775137240",
      "readingUnitId": "c13-s06-p157-02700-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c13-087",
      "parentFingerprint": "a68101c0f5088649ac3120574da8c8f7c4485d804cf5ba7c7c19cabf465e9c4d",
      "passageSha256": "b9587c4a6ff6408d50b736961c08e272ecf9781ced8c9c94e3014ed064e3d2b2",
      "pdfPages": [
        157
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 16,
      "questionId": "qe-c13-0137",
      "sentenceId": "c13-s06-p157-02700-s005",
      "sentenceText": "To be clear, nostalgia—sentimental longing for one’s past—has a number of benefits, ranging from a sense of connection between one’s past and present, to social connectedness, to helping us find meaning in our lives.",
      "sentenceSha256": "13be5d6a2d48b345c4b5c9c13dc563670de29d6bbb16ac7d891da4c3349185d9",
      "readingUnitId": "c13-s06-p157-02700-r005-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c13-088",
      "parentFingerprint": "cb0ca3383724140cd18760fd5c0b5443a4dc7849a1bff9b815c5697ed5a853c7",
      "passageSha256": "075105c38f6d97eb59532f12a68ebabfa9fe61e88e6c28b0f81fc72a78d5e3b0",
      "pdfPages": [
        157
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 17,
      "questionId": "qe-c13-0138",
      "sentenceId": "c13-s06-p157-02700-s006",
      "sentenceText": "However, listening to the same band for the sake of nostalgia does not increase psychological richness.",
      "sentenceSha256": "45e47f317013867cf5800585b9057bc160c0fa66c2eafdbbd10260132ac110ab",
      "readingUnitId": "c13-s06-p157-02700-r005-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c13-088",
      "parentFingerprint": "cb0ca3383724140cd18760fd5c0b5443a4dc7849a1bff9b815c5697ed5a853c7",
      "passageSha256": "075105c38f6d97eb59532f12a68ebabfa9fe61e88e6c28b0f81fc72a78d5e3b0",
      "pdfPages": [
        157
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 18,
      "questionId": "qe-c13-0139",
      "sentenceId": "c13-s07-p157-05745-s001",
      "sentenceText": "Like the Beatles, Virginia Woolf has enthusiastic fans across generations.",
      "sentenceSha256": "9b618cd19a8e107771829602d7fb9286ef52ca5d55ed0929885e131c7b95ac44",
      "readingUnitId": "c13-s07-p157-05745-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c13-089",
      "parentFingerprint": "493b2e53aa765d72a167a74785c4b2a3f76abc0db00f9cdd31363b8745f2fa48",
      "passageSha256": "c1ea491327dd564de9f7c5d74bd065a1bc4559eaec4175e06184b380736855e4",
      "pdfPages": [
        157
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 19,
      "questionId": "qe-c13-0140",
      "sentenceId": "c13-s07-p157-05745-s002",
      "sentenceText": "The novelist Jenny Offill wrote an essay entitled “A Lifetime of Lessons in Mrs. Dalloway” for The New Yorker.",
      "sentenceSha256": "e3ff55b80d490fe98fbd333864ccbd341508389a0f7f7e13fdd4d8238e3dd0b8",
      "readingUnitId": "c13-s07-p157-05745-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c13-089",
      "parentFingerprint": "493b2e53aa765d72a167a74785c4b2a3f76abc0db00f9cdd31363b8745f2fa48",
      "passageSha256": "c1ea491327dd564de9f7c5d74bd065a1bc4559eaec4175e06184b380736855e4",
      "pdfPages": [
        157
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 20,
      "questionId": "qe-c13-0141",
      "sentenceId": "c13-s07-p157-05745-s004",
      "sentenceText": "When she first read it, she was seventeen or eighteen years old.",
      "sentenceSha256": "4ed45d0d3cc69df6c48c02cc757a84ac90b8e6f807e167f7ef1bc7d80b9af87f",
      "readingUnitId": "c13-s07-p157-05745-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c13-089",
      "parentFingerprint": "493b2e53aa765d72a167a74785c4b2a3f76abc0db00f9cdd31363b8745f2fa48",
      "passageSha256": "c1ea491327dd564de9f7c5d74bd065a1bc4559eaec4175e06184b380736855e4",
      "pdfPages": [
        157
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 21,
      "questionId": "qe-c13-0142",
      "sentenceId": "c13-s07-p157-05745-s006",
      "sentenceText": "Woolf introduced him as “aged about thirty, pale-faced, beak-nosed,” adding, “The world has raised its whip; where will it descend?”",
      "sentenceSha256": "93b3c70e7e5bb53f610ad5630c139a0a9050cd52bd03f4667beaafb67b78508d",
      "readingUnitId": "c13-s07-p157-05745-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c13-090",
      "parentFingerprint": "5f0d7435efbe364b00afef9e6fdae5815d48fce609fccf7e915f819331b8bf78",
      "passageSha256": "bcad047f364a7786b23b5b5f0dae01030dcc6f2dd8ccd614824b847837bf4365",
      "pdfPages": [
        157,
        158
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 22,
      "questionId": "qe-c13-0143",
      "sentenceId": "c13-s07-p157-05745-s007",
      "sentenceText": "Offill thought, “Yes, this.",
      "sentenceSha256": "35c3ca80de8b2f64205a287988c127c011d4d5c3437f0a4f1d1cd04ab2ad31f0",
      "readingUnitId": "c13-s07-p157-05745-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c13-090",
      "parentFingerprint": "5f0d7435efbe364b00afef9e6fdae5815d48fce609fccf7e915f819331b8bf78",
      "passageSha256": "bcad047f364a7786b23b5b5f0dae01030dcc6f2dd8ccd614824b847837bf4365",
      "pdfPages": [
        157,
        158
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 23,
      "questionId": "qe-c13-0144",
      "sentenceId": "c13-s07-p157-05745-s008",
      "sentenceText": "Exactly this.”",
      "sentenceSha256": "9a381d16ef684d1ec57e2135a08d85efbcf5bfba7d671cdd5b6fbfdca5a4a705",
      "readingUnitId": "c13-s07-p157-05745-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c13-090",
      "parentFingerprint": "5f0d7435efbe364b00afef9e6fdae5815d48fce609fccf7e915f819331b8bf78",
      "passageSha256": "bcad047f364a7786b23b5b5f0dae01030dcc6f2dd8ccd614824b847837bf4365",
      "pdfPages": [
        157,
        158
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 24,
      "questionId": "qe-c13-0145",
      "sentenceId": "c13-s07-p157-05745-s009",
      "sentenceText": "Then, in her thirties, she read it again.",
      "sentenceSha256": "a7a5230dda7edb728ee532e54db25b02df779a2e6d6ef91c8bbc81ca1dbcd6b5",
      "readingUnitId": "c13-s07-p157-05745-r009-012",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c13-091",
      "parentFingerprint": "b98f88d4186e04205e45e2d7377b424b4f116e13966c196a16ebd655e663bdf7",
      "passageSha256": "b3900db9ad62fde15f34546a4901456ffda3495f6881ae020ea2b773f4a7bb35",
      "pdfPages": [
        158
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 25,
      "questionId": "qe-c13-0146",
      "sentenceId": "c13-s07-p157-05745-s011",
      "sentenceText": "Finally, Offill read it again as she became Mrs. Dalloway’s age, “just broken into her fifty-second year.”",
      "sentenceSha256": "a12aed69f6cc51af2c9f451a338d9a592c01209323242333687bb91dea31d3dc",
      "readingUnitId": "c13-s07-p157-05745-r009-012",
